      "descriptions": {
        "en": {
          "title": "The First Commandment",
          "prompt": "As told in Genesis 1, God creates humanity on the sixth day of creation and charges them to “be fruitful and multiply and fill the earth.” Sefer HaChinukh, the anonymous 13th-century enumeration and explanation of commandments, lists this pronouncement as the first commandment in the Torah and discusses its significance.",
